1
00:00:00,799 --> 00:00:06,079
direction of the farm buildings braying at the top of his voice.

2
00:00:06,079 --> 00:00:11,479
It was the first time that they had ever seen Benjamin excited. Indeed, it was

3
00:00:11,479 --> 00:00:16,840
the first time that anyone had ever seen him gallop.

4
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:21,319
"Quick! Quick! Come at once! They're taking Boxer away!"

5
00:00:21,319 --> 00:00:26,440
Without waiting for orders from the pig, the animals broke off work and raced

6
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:29,360
back to the farm buildings.

7
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:36,280
Sure enough, there in the yard was a large closed van drawn by two horses

8
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:41,879
with lettering on its side and a sly-looking man in a low-crowned bowler

9
00:00:41,879 --> 00:00:45,000
hat sitting on the driver's seat.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,120
And Boxer's stall was empty.

11
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:52,600
The animals crowded round the van.

12
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:55,719
"Goodbye, Boxer!" they chorused.

13
00:00:55,719 --> 00:00:57,319
"Goodbye!"

14
00:00:57,319 --> 00:01:00,280
"Fools! Fools!"

15
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:05,840
shouted Benjamin, prancing round them and stamping the earth with his small hoofs.

16
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:10,399
"Fools! Do you not see what is written on the side of that van?

17
00:01:10,399 --> 00:01:14,760
That gave the animals pause and there was a hush.

18
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:20,120
Muriel began to spell out the words, but Benjamin pushed her aside and in the

19
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:25,879
midst of a deadly silence he read, "Alfred Simmonds, horse slaughterer and

20
00:01:25,879 --> 00:01:31,959
glue boiler, Willington. Dealer in hides and bone meal. Kennels supplied.

21
00:01:31,959 --> 00:01:34,120
Do you not understand what that means?

22
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,719
They are taking Boxer to the knackers."

23
00:01:36,719 --> 00:01:40,360
A cry of horror burst from all the animals.

24
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:44,920
At this moment the man on the box whipped up his horses and the van moved

25
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:48,120
out of the yard at a smart trot.

26
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:52,600
All the animals followed, crying out at the tops of their voices.

27
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,319
Clover forced her way to the front.

28
00:01:55,319 --> 00:01:58,399
The van began to gather speed.

29
00:01:58,399 --> 00:02:03,399
Clover tried to stir her stout limbs to a gallop and achieved a canter.

30
00:02:03,399 --> 00:02:05,200
Boxer!

31
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,120
She cried.

32
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:11,040
Boxer! Boxer! Boxer!

33
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:15,840
And just at this moment, as though he had heard the uproar outside, Boxer's

34
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:20,440
face, with the white stripe down his nose, appeared at the small window at

35
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:22,239
the back of the van.

36
00:02:22,239 --> 00:02:23,520
Boxer!

37
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:29,040
Boxer, get out! Get out quickly! They are taking you to your death!

38
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:34,440
All the animals took up the cry of, "Get out, Boxer! Get out!"

39
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:38,639
But the van was already gathering speed and drawing away from them.

40
00:02:38,639 --> 00:02:42,520
It was uncertain whether Boxer had understood what Clover had said, but a

41
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:46,799
moment later, his face disappeared from the window, and there was the sound of a

42
00:02:46,799 --> 00:02:50,719
tremendous drumming of hooves inside the van.

43
00:02:50,719 --> 00:02:53,360
He was trying to kick his way out.

44
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:59,479
The time had been when a few kicks from Boxer's hooves would have smashed the van to matchwood.

45
00:02:59,479 --> 00:03:02,280
But alas, his strength had left him.

46
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:08,239
And in a few moments, the sound of drumming hooves grew fainter and died away.

47
00:03:08,239 --> 00:03:14,680
In desperation, the animals began appealing to the two horses which drew the van to stop.

48
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:16,959
Comrades! Comrades!

49
00:03:16,959 --> 00:03:20,000
Don't take your own brother to his death!

50
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,840
But the stupid brutes, too ignorant to realize what was happening, merely set

51
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:28,479
back their ears and quickened their pace.

52
00:03:28,479 --> 00:03:30,000
Boxer's face did not reappear at the
